    <field name="scopecontent_teim">Borden Parker Bowne (January 14, 1847, Leonardville, NJ – April 1, 1910, Boston, MA) was an American Christian philosopher and theologian in the Methodist tradition. In 1876, Bowne became a professor of philosophy at Boston University, where he taught for more than thirty years; he later served as dean of the graduate school. Bowne&#39;s published works are available at New York University Libraries via Bobcat. </field>
